CHAPTER.VERS:
And Yahweh said to the sons of Israel, [Did] not [I save you

          {+}
        ] from the Egyptians, and from the Amorites, from the sons of Ammon, and from the Philistines?

The Sidonians also, and the Amalekites, and the Maonites, had oppressed you

          {+}
        ; and you

          {+}
         cried to me, and I saved you

          {+}
         out of their hand.

Yet you

          {+}
         have forsaken me, and served other gods: therefore I will save you

          {+}
         no more.

Go and cry to the gods which you

          {+}
         have chosen; let them save you

          {+}
         in the time of your

          {+}
         distress.
